Fixture patch for the patches/ overlay self-test.  Adds a sentinel comment to
the fixture source.  It is a git-style diff on purpose: a `diff --git` patch
applied from a subdirectory of a work tree is exactly what git silently SKIPS
without the apply-time isolation, so this file reproduces the original bug in
the negative leg of the self-test.  (git apply ignores this free-text preamble
and starts at the `diff --git` line below.)

diff --git a/src/hello.c b/src/hello.c
--- a/src/hello.c
+++ b/src/hello.c
@@ -11,5 +11,6 @@
 int
 chimera_patch_selftest_fixture(void)
 {
+    /* CHIMERA_PATCH_SELFTEST_SENTINEL: proves the overlay patch landed */
     return 0;
 }
